The `@example` block shows bare assignment expressions (`deviceAddons = ['@storybook/addon-ondevice-controls'];`) rather than the field as a property within a config object literal. This is syntactically incorrect as a standalone statement and inconsistent with how other `@example` blocks in this file are written. It should use the full config context:
```ts
export default {
  deviceAddons: ['@storybook/addon-ondevice-controls'],
};
```

Per project coding guidelines, all `vi.mock()` calls must include the `{ spy: true }` option. This call is missing it:
```ts
vi.mock('../helpers/mainConfigFile', { spy: true }, () => ({
  updateMainConfig: mocks.updateMainConfig,
}));
```

The `prompt()` method receives a `PromptOptions<RnOndeviceAddonsOptions>` argument (which includes `result.ondeviceAddons`) but ignores it entirely. The message would be more actionable if it listed the specific addon names that will be moved, e.g.:
```ts
prompt({ result }) {
  const names = result.ondeviceAddons.map(getAddonName).join(', ');
  return `We detected on-device addons (${names}) in your \`addons\` config. ...`;
},
```
